const builtInCampaigns=[{"id": "dead-signal", "name": "Dead Signal", "meet": "ds-kara", "party": ["ds-rook", "ds-sera"], "plan": {"premise": "A bounty-hunter crew answers an SOS and finds you alone on a drifting ship with no memory. They carry you to a dead station, and as your memories return you realize it is the place you escaped, where the company is growing a living weapon.", "genre": "Horror", "shape": "", "intro": "Your small ship drifts alone in the dark, its beacon crying SOS. You wake in a cold pod as a bounty-hunter crew cuts through the hull. You don't remember your name. Only one image: a white corridor, red light, running.", "chapters": ["The crew takes you aboard. Kara, their chief, decides you are crew until proven otherwise. Unit Seven, the android medic, checks you over while everyone watches the android, not you.", "Rook reads your beacon: the SOS carries a recovery order, return craft and occupant to point of origin, reward paid on delivery. A station, not far. The job pays well, so they set course. You feel sick and don't know why. Memory: the station's name on a door sign. You have read it before.", "The dead station. Docking, no lights, no people, every door sealed. Then the sounds: slow booms deep inside, something skittering through the walls. The crew hears it too.", "Locked out. Every door to the bridge is sealed and you only ever hear the thing, never see it. Unit Seven crawls into the vents alone, into the same ducts the skittering comes from, to open the doors from the other side. It makes it. Kara stops watching it like a threat.", "Power on. To go on you must restore power. Rook throws the main breaker and one switch unspools everything: lights flicker up, every door unlocks both ways, an old alarm wails over a company message, and something on the lower decks answers. Memory: you know this alarm, and the way to the labs without a map.", "The labs. The logs show the species being bred as a weapon. Unit Seven finds Lyra Voss, half rebuilt by the company with machine parts, a woman the scans say is dead, and carries her out when everyone else wants to leave her. Memory: you worked here, you tried to free the test subjects, and they caught you.", "The twist. It all comes back: you escaped this station, and your own SOS carried you straight back to it. Director Hale comes on comms and knows your name. The crew had no idea; they are on your side, and now they are targets too.", "The betrayal. Hale offers the crew a fortune for you and Lyra. Sera Vale, ten years on the crew and Kara's oldest friend, takes it, sure one deal fixes everything. She seals the crew away from the ship and tells Kara she is saving them. It saves no one: Hale opens the pens anyway.", "The big fight. The hunt breaks loose. Lyra holds the line alone so everyone can reach the ship and loses her legs and an arm doing it. The door closes on her. Everyone believes she is gone, and so does she.", "Lifting off, the station's core going critical. Then static on comms, and inside it Lyra's voice, crying alone. Everyone looks at you: it's too dangerous, she's as good as dead. Kara: with you to the end. You: turn the ship around. Dex: it's going to blow, we'll never make it back out. He turns the ship around anyway."], "conclusion": "Unit Seven goes in for Lyra while the core counts down, the machine carrying the woman who thought she was only a machine. Everyone who chose to come back gets out with her, and what you do with the proof of Hale's program decides how it ends."}}];
